# Pipeline environment (server-side only).
#
# This file lists the keys the offline pipeline reads. Copy it to pipeline/.env
# and fill real values there. The real .env is git-ignored (see root .gitignore:
# "pipeline/.env"). None of these values belong in the app bundle or in any
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable. See CLAUDE.md > Secrets.
#
# Every key is optional. Without one, its stage is skipped and the free stages
# (Datamuse, Open English WordNet, export) still run. With --dry-run the
# pipeline makes no network calls at all and writes only to pipeline/out/.

# --- Anthropic Claude (batch generation, stage 03) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key

# --- Google Gemini (alternative for stage 03) ---
# Used only when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set. Key from Google AI Studio.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# Optional: models to try in order for each request, comma-separated.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash,gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# --- Text to speech (stage 04) ---
# Kokoro, an open voice model that runs on this computer: no key needed. Set up
# its Python env once (README > Audio). Optional overrides:
# KOKORO_VOICE=af_heart
# KOKORO_PYTHON=/Users/you/.cache/little-lexicon-tts/.venv/bin/python

# --- Supabase (learners' reports, curate.ts reports and resolve) ---
# The games-apps project URL and its service role key. The key bypasses row
# level security, so it must never leave this file.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
